 # 38. Conceptual Principles
 
-The Classification concepts are governed by the following principles:
+All seven original principle headings remain with the actual current subject, owner and evidence boundaries below. They are scoped working conceptual requirements, not new AP identifiers or proof of implementation.
+
+---
 
 ## 38.1. Semantic Independence
 
-Classification represents semantic organization rather than physical organization.
+Classification meaning is semantic rather than directory/storage meaning. Physical arrangements can reflect a category without defining it; actual assignment/reference/provider effects still need applicable evidence.
+
+---
 
 ## 38.2. Explicit Meaning
 
-Every classification concept shall have an explicit meaning.
+Use explicit responsible definition/source/edition/context for actual concepts. Labels or aliases alone do not establish identity, meaning or valid usage; no complete vocabulary or missing Model is invented.
+
+---
 
 ## 38.3. Controlled Vocabulary
 
-Classification values shall belong to defined semantic categories.
+Actual admitted values/categories and usage follow responsible definitions and scheme/schema/lifecycle/constraints context. A Dictionary listing alone is not complete population, approval or actual assignment evidence.
+
+---
 
 ## 38.4. Separation of Responsibilities
 
-Classification shall remain distinct from Identity, Metadata, Storage, Governance and Discovery.
+Classification category/assignment meanings remain distinct from document identity, Metadata representation, Storage execution, Governance common process and Discovery capabilities. Distinction does not erase actual indispensable provider interfaces or Classification's own governance/validation conditions; authorized executor and CMS scope remain separate.
+
+---
 
 ## 38.5. Stable Identity
 
-Classification changes shall not implicitly change Document Identity.
+Ordinary classification change does not reconstruct governing assigned document K or its same-document association. Mutable support/assignment/definition records and other entity identities differ. Necessary assessed governing revision needs §33 authority/mappings/history/reference/snapshot evidence; no arbitrary reassignment or silent retargeting.
+
+---
 
 ## 38.6. Technology Independence
 
-Classification concepts shall not depend on implementation technologies.
+Conceptual meaning is independent of a particular technology while actual logical formats, representations, provider interfaces, authority, provenance and performed checks remain applicable. No content-free checker, universally harmless migration or installed adapter is inferred.
+
+---
 
 ## 38.7. Extensibility
 
-Classification concepts shall support controlled evolution.
+Ordinary compatible addition preserves applicable interpretation; necessary assessed normative/role/interface/foundational/domain revision follows §33 with real authority/impact/version/mappings/history/transition checks. The word extension alone grants no fake compatibility, additional Type or implicit canonical field.
 
